        <item>
            <title>1.3.0</title>
            <pubDate>Sun, 19 Jul 2026 11:04:14 -0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>18</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.3.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>
  :root { color-scheme: light dark; }
  body { font: -apple-system-body, system-ui, sans-serif; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 0 0 0.5em; }
  ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2em; }
  li { margin: 0.35em 0; }
  strong { font-weight: 600; }
</style>

<h2>What's New in Lineform 1.3.0</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Document tabs</strong> — keep several files open in one window and switch between them without losing your place.</li>
  <li><strong>Images in Read and Preview</strong> — local images now render inline instead of showing a placeholder, and they appear in Styled PDF and print output. If an image has moved, a Reconnect button relinks it.</li>
  <li><strong>Syntax highlighting in code blocks</strong>, with a hover button to copy a block's contents.</li>
  <li><strong>Callouts</strong> — <code>&gt; [!NOTE]</code>, <code>[!TIP]</code>, <code>[!IMPORTANT]</code>, <code>[!WARNING]</code>, and <code>[!CAUTION]</code> blocks render with their own title row.</li>
  <li><strong>Jump to File (⌘K)</strong> — fuzzy-search your workspace and open any file instantly.</li>
  <li><strong>Search across every file</strong> — the new All Files scope shows matching lines from your whole workspace, and clicking a result opens that file.</li>
  <li><strong>Read aloud</strong> — Edit ▸ Speech reads the document (or your selection) out loud.</li>
  <li><strong>Export As ▸ Rich Text</strong>, plus a style picker for PDF export and printing.</li>
  <li><strong>Markdown previews in Finder</strong> — press Space on a <code>.md</code> file to see it rendered the way Lineform renders it.</li>
  <li><strong>Shortcuts support</strong> — New Note and Open in Lineform are now available to Shortcuts, Spotlight, and Siri.</li>
  <li><strong>⌘E</strong> toggles between Write and Read, and your scroll position carries across the switch.</li>
  <li><strong>Pie charts in Mermaid diagrams</strong>, and unsupported diagram types now fail cleanly instead of rendering nonsense.</li>
  <li>A redesigned tab bar and window chrome that follow your reading theme in both light and dark mode.</li>
  <li><strong>Fixes:</strong> closed two Save As paths that could lose work, a file can no longer be open in two windows at once, switching to a tab whose file changed on disk now reloads it instead of showing a stale copy, and text no longer jumps while you resize the window.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
